    <h1>Webflow vs. <em>a custom-coded site built to bring in calls</em></h1>
    <p>Webflow is the most credible of the visual builders. Professional designers use it, and its output is clean. For a service business, the comparison comes down to leads, local search, and long-term cost.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container prose" style="max-width:980px">

    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Where Webflow is the right call</h2>
    <p>Webflow is the no-code builder I respect most. It suits portfolios, marketing-led software companies, design firms, and agencies, where design and animation sell more than Google's map results do. It does these things well:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Speed.</strong> Webflow sites typically score 75&ndash;90 on Google's speed test for phones, well ahead of Wix and Squarespace.</li>
      <li><strong>Design.</strong> A skilled designer can produce original work in Webflow.</li>
      <li><strong>Editing.</strong> Owners can make small edits in the browser without breaking the site.</li>
      <li><strong>Animation.</strong> Its interactions panel does what would otherwise need a developer.</li>
      <li><strong>Code export.</strong> Webflow can export a site's code, without the content you manage in its editor (the CMS) or its forms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where Webflow costs you leads</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Speed short of the top.</strong> Custom code scores 95&ndash;100. The gap between 85 and 98 is smaller than the gap from Wix, but it still changes how many phone visitors leave.</li>
      <li><strong>Less local search control.</strong> Webflow's business details for Google (schema) allow less control on each page than hand-written markup, which matters in Google's map results (the "local pack").</li>
      <li><strong>Prices that rise with traffic.</strong> Webflow's CMS and Business plans run $30&ndash;$50 a month, with bandwidth limits on the lower tiers.</li>
      <li><strong>Specialist skills.</strong> Good Webflow work needs a Webflow specialist; custom-code skills are broader and more transferable.</li>
      <li><strong>Forms that run through Webflow.</strong> Sending submissions to your email or customer software takes a higher tier or an outside connector.</li>
    </ul>

